+P25 — matrix-verified separable Cartesian curl-curl candidate subspace
+
+No case-name or metadata dispatch, reference input, answer table, or full dense matrix in the solver.
+The recognizer derives dimensions from CSR row 0, then verifies every CSR row, column and value.
+B must be positive diagonal and constant within each of the three inferred edge blocks, or I.
+The supported natural ordering has block shapes (Nx,Ny-1,Nz-1), (Nx-1,Ny,Nz-1), (Nx-1,Ny-1,Nz), each dimension >=3.
+Coefficients alpha are derived from actual transverse off-diagonal entries. Expected diagonal,
+same-component neighboring entries and all cross-component +/- entries are checked with a fixed
+128 epsilon * largest expected coefficient gate. Unexpected sparsity or nonuniform values reject.
+This comparison is a candidate-generation gate, NOT a proof of exact separability or completeness.
+
+For node-to-cell difference D with +1 at (j,j), -1 at (j+1,j), the normalized pencil is:
+H_dd = sum_(e!=d) alpha_e D_e^T D_e, acting along transverse node axes;
+H_de = -sqrt(alpha_d alpha_e) D_d D_e^T, identities along the remaining axis.
+For wave numbers m_d in [0,N_d), use normalized node sine and cell cosine bases. In a mode,
+s_d=2 sqrt(alpha_d) sin(m_d*pi/(2*N_d)), and the 3-component block is ||s||^2 I-s s^T.
+Three nonzero wave numbers give two transverse polarizations; exactly two give one polarization
+along the zero wave-number axis. The remaining gradient modes are zero. Construct X in physical
+coordinates by B^-1/2. Only requests whose nearest set excludes the null space and does not split
+an unresolved boundary multiplet use this candidate path. All other requests use the old driver.
+
+After candidate construction, actual A*X and B*X, rank-revealing Rayleigh-Ritz and actual backward
+errors are evaluated. If rank != k or any error > 0.5*original tol, discard candidates and run the
+original factorization/Lanczos path. On acceptance skip only the main numerical factorization and
+Krylov iteration. Symbolic analysis, memory planning, original final verification, exact double
+Sylvester counts, missing-pair reruns and final success criteria remain. The model spectrum is
+only an endpoint hint; it never replaces the actual exact counts. Public final tolerance unchanged.
+
+Private experimental toggle P25_STRUCTURE=1. Built from current P20 production library, not P21.
+Only definite.cpp is replaced in a copied archive. Native and P21 binaries retained for comparison.
+Exact certificate mode required for this private candidate path. No production adoption yet.
+
